{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/144093-redeeming-slashers","id":144093,"title":"Redeeming Slashers.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-20T21:27:17-07:00","id":144093,"title":"Redeeming Slashers.","content":"Does a Slasher whos Morality, increases to 5, lose his undertaking and any associated traits?<br /> <br /> Never explicitly says that, and with &quot;Freak&quot; it might be hard to justify... otherwise it seems self explanatory to me, at least...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T13:48:48-07:00","id":144822,"title":"","content":"It's an interesting idea, but I would think not. In my mind, a Slasher has not so much &quot;fallen&quot; as<br /> evolved (or devolved if you prefer). As such, they would likely have a Code (The Code, HtV pg 322)<br /> that is highly specialized and specific. It might even be in the 5-7 range for some Avengers. The<br /> disturbing fact about Slashers is that they willingly entered into their existence (usually). Rarely<br /> did they set out to become as bad (or worse) than the monsters they hunted, but the choice to<br /> step over a line was made. Again and again.<br /> <br /> Now having said all that, I would think trying to save someone becoming a Slasher could make<br /> an excellent story with the right group. If they succeed, that person could be grateful or highly<br /> resentful. If they fail, it could begin a longer running affair with someone that is the monster<br /> in the mirror. This recurring villain knows their strategies and their likely targets because s/he<br /> uses them as well. And after that first contact, perhaps The Code changed again... to include<br /> the Hunters.<br /> <br /> It's a wonderful story arc with great possibilities no matter how things turn out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":2668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","user":"Asmenedas","date":".  Spacing tried to divide by 0. 05-21-2014, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T03:24:06-07:00","id":145470,"title":"","content":"I would say that Rippers could be saved with normal medicine and therapy; or quite quickly with supernatural medicine. Scourges are too far gone, and have the usual no removing a template rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T11:40:03-07:00","id":145861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/144093-redeeming-slashers?p=145470#post145470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that Rippers could be saved with normal medicine and therapy; or quite quickly with supernatural medicine. Scourges are too far gone, and have the usual no removing a template rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I can agree with this as well. Though trying to reach a Scourge could be an interesting story. Maybe have<br /> &quot;breakthrough moments&quot; where one of the characters convinces her/him to stay their hand through reminders of<br /> who they were... only to have them relapse violently (for them) after they come to their senses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T22:46:42-07:00","id":147628,"title":"","content":"There's a scene in many of the more horror-oriented slasher movies about scourges when one of the characters thinks they've managed to get through to the superkiller, only to be killed viciously once they've let down their guard.<br /> <br /> The rehabilitation does seem to be something in stories targeted towards the more ripper type killers. It usually doesn't end well, with them relapsing horribly, being abused because they can't fight back, or dying saving someone else. Of course that could be a good story. Occasionally they manage to get their interests focused in another direction so that they can, while not actively participate in investigations, occasionally act in an advisory position (like Hannibal Lecter, I guess, though in comics I believe a few have made their way into politics and become members of things comparable to Hunter agencies, as they've 'seen the light' or manage to sublimate their urge to kill into more socially acceptable things.<br /> <br /> I like the above poster's suggestion of allowing it for rippers, but not for scourges, as the supernatural element would endure anything done to them. But that doesn't mean players can't try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:58:59-07:00","id":163052,"title":"","content":"The way it was explained to me, Scourges are people who have utterly lost touch with society. The only connection they have to it anymore is to kill, and kill, and kill. As such, I feel it would / should be impossible to restore a Scourge. That kind of damage likely comes from extreme trauma which might render them to a point where they no longer want to be restored. They find comfort in what they've become, it's the only thing that keeps them alive anymore when they lose everything they've loved or believed in.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Rippers, on the other hand, are typical psychopaths and with therapy, medicine, and strict supervision might be able to be restored at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T19:20:34-07:00","id":163060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/144093-redeeming-slashers?p=163052#post163052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rippers, on the other hand, are typical psychopaths and with therapy, medicine, and strict supervision might be able to be restored at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>A mix of psychopaths and junkie. Slashers have the urge to kill the same way a junkie needs a fix and even if you manage to rehab the slasher where he isn't psychopathic anymore, he still feels the urge to kill every so often.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T23:42:16-07:00","id":163224,"title":"","content":"Compacts and conspiracies, among other books I believe, talks about curing monsters.<br /> <br /> If a hunter can cure someone of being a blood drinking corpse or being a technoorganic quantum entity than curing a psychopath, even one with supernatural features, seems easy in comparison.<br /> <br /> But seeming easy when compared to epic really doesn't say much. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:15:24-07:00","id":163654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/144093-redeeming-slashers?p=145470#post145470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that Rippers could be saved with normal medicine and therapy; or quite quickly with supernatural medicine. Scourges are too far gone, and have the usual no removing a template rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>A rule, I may politely point out, got a nifty &quot;ignore this&quot; mentioned in Compacts and Conspiracies for certain stories.<br /> <br /> I mean, as a general rule, it's absolutely true, but when the writer's themselves discuss the possibilities of hunters doing just that, it helps to remember that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T18:26:09-07:00","id":173436,"title":"","content":"Probably not too farfetched for Freaks and Avengers who have oddly justifiable motivations. Unlikely for Masks and Legends who are too far gone and barely human at that point. With Geniuses you can probably cooperate if they see what's in it for them, but it'll most likely backfire at some point. Like I said, it's situational, but the Ripper vs. Scourge rule is an okay rule of thumb, but I think it depends on the individual more than anything else. The template removal thing is probably hard to justify in either case, but flavorwise, whatever works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3309-electrick","name":"electrick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}